
It is pitch black in these catacombs.
You have a magickal spell that lists all items in a room.

To see in the dark, type:     ls
To move around, type:         cd `directory`

MAGICKAL VIEWING SPELLS:

To see room contents:         ls              (list all items)
To view scrolls fully:        cat `filename`  (display entire scroll)
To read long scrolls:         less `filename` (page through text, 'q' to quit)
To peek at scroll start:      head `filename` (see first 10 lines)
To check scroll ending:       tail `filename` (see last 10 lines)
To count scroll contents:     wc `filename`   (count lines, words, characters)

Try looking around this room.
Then move into one of the next rooms.

EXAMPLE INCANTATIONS:

$ ls
$ cat scroll
$ less scroll
$ head scroll
$ tail scroll
$ wc scroll
$ cd cellar

Remember to cast these spells when you discover new scrolls and treasures!

=== THE FIRST CHALLENGE ===

Before you venture deeper into the catacombs, you must prove your mastery
of the viewing spells. Practice reading this very scroll with different
commands to understand their power.

When you're ready, seek the CELLAR - a chamber that lies beneath this entrance.
The cellar holds ancient secrets about seeing through illusions and
distinguishing between doorways and objects.

Use your navigation spell to descend: cd cellar

May your terminal skills grow strong, brave adventurer!